FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] tests/common/vm.rs:415 — `edge_a_limit_left_in_the_environment_cannot_change_an_outcome` calls `std::env::set_var`/`remove_var` on process-global `REDBLUE_MAX_*` while cargo runs tests in parallel and never restores prior values — flaky cross-test pollution for any test using `Vm::new()` — and it only checks `tree_walk` before vs after, never `bytecode` under pollution, so a bytecode env leak passes — fix by serializing env access with a mutex/guard that restores originals and asserting both `tree_walk` and `bytecode` are unchanged.
2. [MAJOR] tests/common/corpus.rs:199 — `record` stores program value as `value.to_string()` and `compare` checks `value.to_string()==recorded.value`, but `src/value.rs:194` renders `Text` bare so `Number(5)` vs `Text("5")` and `Nothing` vs `Text("nothing")` collide to the same `#value` line — a type-confusion regression passes the golden check — fix by recording a type-tagged value (`Debug` or `type:value`) instead of `Display`.
3. [MAJOR] tests/differential_test.rs:361 — `edge_a_generated_program_only_faults_on_a_fault_that_was_injected` asserts only `outcome.result.is_err()` for `Some(fault)`, never that the failure matches the injected tail — a prefix-statement defect that faults for another reason still passes the `with_fault` arm — fix by asserting the failure label/message/position equals the fault tail run alone.
4. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/vm.rs:361 — `line_span` returns `Span::new(line,1)` for every instruction and `src/vm.rs:550` reports statement granularity, so every runtime failure is `line:1` (pinned at `tests/common/vm.rs:379` as `Span::new(3,1)`) — the `#position` column comparison can never vary and a column move is invisible — fix by threading expression spans into both VMs or dropping the column from the claimed coverage.
5. [MAJOR] tests/common/generator.rs:963 — `edge_every_kind_is_reachable_and_its_arms_produce_it` runs 30 seeds per `Kind` and asserts each run is `Ok`, but never asserts each `expression` arm was taken, so a dead/unreachable arm passes silently — fix by counting arm hits (instrument or replicate `rng.below` choices) and asserting each arm fired.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
